    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point, boasting a 72.40 efficiency score. His favorable platoon edge against Dotel, coupled with a lead-off spot in the order, provides the highest ceiling for stolen base production, our most critical scarcity target. While **Josh Smith** (62.54) and **Caleb Durbin** (61.84) also project strongly against the hittable matchup provided by Bassitt, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains the anchor of the lineup given his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the premium value we assign to his elite speed. \n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, most notably the matchup for **Junior Caminero**, whose score was depressed to 49.84 by a difficult outing against Ullola (2.27 xERA). Despite this, we are holding firm because our bench depth is currently limited; **Chase Meidroth** (50.86) was our closest consideration, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his utility against Liberatore did not provide enough categorical upside to warrant displacing the higher projected raw outputs of our starters. We are also monitoring the heavy workload for **Trea Turner**, who faces a high-caliber arm in Sale; while his score of 53.65 is respectable, the elite SP skill (-19%) necessitates caution, even as his batting order position (#2) keeps him firmly in our plans. \n\nFinally, be advised that **Dillon Dingler** (39.33) has fallen below our 40.0 efficiency floor, rendering him unplayable today regardless of his BvP historicals. With **Yordan Alvarez** and **Gary Sanchez** unavailable due to lineup status, the burden of production rests on **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** to capitalize on the favorable 5.10 xERA of Scherzer. The squad remains optimized to prioritize stolen base opportunities while navigating these specific pitching hurdles; maintain focus on the 5x5 categories as we look to close the gap in the Roto standings.",
